{"title":"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Cynthia graphs a sequence of points. The first point has coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f6de6ae1cd7c59d7ffcc74f695904b8f8d1d3e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-3, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, the second point has coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d77f6629a03324c8d886ed383a47e8f090b71de6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, and the third point has coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f9ba91b378b33b75a172e77e70e8396ff92f641.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />. Each point after the first is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unit to the right and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units above the previous point. What is the fourth point that Cynthia graphs?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b3364adb67b5949273c76b9ce91b79b8fce7e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ (1, 5) \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ (-4, -2) \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ (2, 6) \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ (0, 5) \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ (0, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"573\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because every point is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the right and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> above the previous point and the third point was at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f9ba91b378b33b75a172e77e70e8396ff92f641.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, the next point must be at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7e0f1e15fdf81e504794d0754b7abf16341f6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1 + 1, 4 + 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>This simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7ae34280b5452fbb29480a86a3d18f03c6e111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } (0, 6)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"87\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28using_the_line.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(using_the_line)\">Solution 2 (using the line)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (using the line)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the fact that the slope would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ec6788809c809c37a6bbb42482510ca5118471e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{1} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" /> according to the fact that each type <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We can then use:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d878515c30bb28e0ea37da6611fc38ccc6f8ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2x + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the y-intercept of the line that would connect all of the points.\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d4c38a419ae56f13a202216dd45a1978bc91a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61a79da7e7844d252be666cb25e2ed8a2c9a96e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> (we could also use any of the other known coordinates), we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/1488aa5f0fe1b312660375bdeddc784ff06d5752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 = 2 \\times -1 + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/211f2b957832e63955b51f02a1ff69a191199403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b - 2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffeba1deaf96010fffb0a80375648dd058eeac85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2 + 4 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the right of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the y-intercept according to the line would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the point that we are looking for is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7ae34280b5452fbb29480a86a3d18f03c6e111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } (0, 6)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"87\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal (page does not exist)\">2025 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <